    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first settlers arrived in June 1799, making Atwater one of the earliest townships established in the Connecticut Western Reserve.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.atwatertwp.net/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Cleveland & Pittsburg Railroad cuts through Atwater’s center, a reminder of the town’s 19th‑century rail connections.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://portage.ohgenweb.org/hist001.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Atwater’s borders touch Edinburg to the north, Stark County to the south, Deerfield to the east, and Randolph to the west.",
